#: PART2.md:1
msgid "Part 2: Design a barrier-flattening potential"
msgstr "Part 2：Barrier を平坦化する Potential の設計"

#: PART2.md:3
msgid ""
"Now that we have a clear picture about the free-energy surface (FES) we can "
"devise a strategy to accelerate the dynamics along the most probable "
"reaction pathway."
msgstr ""
"自由エネルギー表面 (FES) が明確になったので、最も確率の高い Reaction Pathway に沿う Dynamics "
"を加速する戦略を立てられます。"

#: PART2.md:5
msgid ""
"The idea behind this approach is to lower the free energy barrier between "
"the bound and the unbound states in the hope of increasing the reaction rate"
" in both directions. In the language of transition state theory (TST), this "
"corresponds to decreasing the (Gibbs) free energy of activation for both the"
" forward and backward processes ($\\Delta^\\ddagger G_\\pm$) in order to "
"increase the corresponding rate constants,"
msgstr ""
"この方法では、結合・非結合状態の間の自由エネルギー Barrier を下げ、両方向の Reaction Rate の増加を狙います。Transition"
" State Theory (TST) では、正逆両過程の活性化 Gibbs 自由エネルギー ($\\Delta^\\ddagger G_\\pm$) "
"を下げ、対応する Rate Constant を上げることに相当します。"

#: PART2.md:13
msgid ""
"We will use the FES previously computed to craft a barrier-flattening bias. "
"For this, no further simulation is needed as we can directly predict the "
"shape of the FES for any bias potential that is a function of the same "
"variables,"
msgstr ""
"先ほどの FES を使い、Barrier を平坦化する Bias を作ります。同じ変数の関数である任意の BiasPotential に対し、FES "
"の形を直接予測できるため、追加のシミュレーションは不要です。"

#: PART2.md:21
msgid "Choosing a functional form"
msgstr "関数形の選択"

#: PART2.md:23
msgid ""
"The choice of $U_\\text{bias}$ is rather free, but we need to take some "
"constraints into account:"
msgstr "$U_\\text{bias}$ は比較的自由に選べますが、次の制約を考慮します。"

#: PART2.md:24
msgid "It should be continuous"
msgstr "連続であること。"

#: PART2.md:25
msgid ""
"Far away from the barrier, the bias should be flat so as to minimally affect"
" the thermodynamic ensemble"
msgstr "Thermodynamic Ensemble への影響を最小限にするため、Barrier から離れた場所では Bias が平坦であること。"

#: PART2.md:26
msgid "The bias should avoid creating stable intermediates"
msgstr "安定な中間体を作らないこと。"

#: PART2.md:28 PART2.md:74 PART2.md:150
msgid "Instructions"
msgstr "演習の手順"

#: PART2.md:30
msgid "Propose a candidate functional form matching the above criteria."
msgstr "以上を満たす関数形の候補を提案してください。"

#: PART2.md:32
msgid ""
"[!TIP] Tip 1 Try to transform the input variables so as to make it easier to"
" fit the barrier with common functions (exp, cos, polynomials, etc.)"
msgstr ""
"[!TIP] ヒント1：一般的な関数（exp、cos、多項式など）で Barrier を Fit しやすいよう、入力変数を変換してみてください。"

#: PART2.md:35
msgid ""
"[!TIP] Tip 2 Use Heaviside step functions to restrict the bias to the "
"section of the CV-space you are interested in. Make sure the resulting "
"potential is continuous (and it’s probably a good idea if it’s "
"differentiable too) everywhere the system can go."
msgstr ""
"[!TIP] ヒント2：Heaviside Step Function で、対象の CV 領域に Bias "
"を限定してください。系が到達できるすべての場所で Potential が連続であることを確認します。微分可能にもしておくとよいでしょう。"

#: PART2.md:38
msgid ""
"Using the reweighted FES computed in [Part 1](PART1.md), predict the shape "
"of the biased FES and plot it."
msgstr ""
"[Part 1](PART1.md) で Reweighting した FES を使い、Bias を加えた FES の形を予測して描画してください。"

#: PART2.md:40
msgid ""
"Adjust the parameters and/or the functional form until you are satisfied "
"with the resulting free-energy barrier."
msgstr "自由エネルギー Barrier が望む形になるまで、パラメータや関数形を調整してください。"

#: PART2.md:42 PART2.md:118
msgid "Results"
msgstr "結果"

#: PART2.md:44
msgid ""
"Here is our proposition. For convenience, we defined new variables $X$ and "
"$Y$ as:"
msgstr "ここで提案する形を示します。便宜上、新しい変数 $X$、$Y$ を次のように定義しました。"

#: PART2.md:53
msgid ""
"where $X$ can be interpreted as the advancement of the "
"O<sub>W</sub>/O<sub>P</sub> exchange ($X = 0$ is the unbound state, $X = 1$ "
"represents the addition of O<sub>P</sub> to the inner-sphere, and $X = 2$ "
"complete departure of the supranumerary O<sub>W</sub> atom) and $Y$ is the "
"excess coordination relative to the basal $n = 6$."
msgstr ""
"$X$ は O<sub>W</sub>/O<sub>P</sub> 交換の進行度と解釈できます。$X = 0$ は非結合状態、$X = 1$ は "
"Inner Sphere への O<sub>P</sub> の追加、$X = 2$ は余分な O<sub>W</sub> 原子の完全な離脱です。$Y$ "
"は基準の $n = 6$ に対する過剰な Coordination です。"

#: PART2.md:55
msgid "![Bias design figure](solutions/figures/bias_design_xy.png)"
msgstr "![Bias の設計](solutions/figures/bias_design_xy.png)"

#: PART2.md:65
msgid "![Bias design figure](solutions/figures/bias_design_XY.png)"
msgstr "![Bias の設計](solutions/figures/bias_design_XY.png)"

#: PART2.md:68
msgid ""
"Your solution will probably look different, and that's OK since precise "
"shape of the barrier should not matter too much."
msgstr "自分の解答が異なる形でも問題ありません。Barrier の厳密な形は、それほど重要ではないはずです。"

#: PART2.md:70
msgid "Testing the barrier-flattening bias"
msgstr "Barrier を平坦化する Bias のテスト"

#: PART2.md:72
msgid ""
"Once you are satisfied with functional form of your bias, you can implement "
"it in a Plumed file."
msgstr "Bias の関数形が決まったら、Plumed 入力に実装します。"

#: PART2.md:76
msgid ""
"Prepare a new directory for the bias testing simulation (you can reuse the "
"same input files as previously)."
msgstr "Bias テスト用に新しいディレクトリを用意してください。前と同じ入力ファイルを再利用できます。"

#: PART2.md:78
msgid ""
"Write a `plumed_bias.dat` file implementing the chosen bias. You will to "
"define a [`CUSTOM`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_c_u_s_t_o_m.html) collective variable and turn its output value "
"into a biasing potential with "
"[`BIASVALUE`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_b_i_a_s_v_a_l_u_e.html)."
msgstr ""
"選んだ Bias を実装する `plumed_bias.dat` "
"を作ります。[`CUSTOM`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_c_u_s_t_o_m.html) Collective Variable を定義し、その出力を "
"[`BIASVALUE`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_b_i_a_s_v_a_l_u_e.html) で BiasPotential にします。"

#: PART2.md:80
msgid ""
"To avoid wasting time with free diffusion of the ion in the simulation box, "
"restrain the Mg<sup>2+</sup> in the vicinity of the O<sub>P</sub> atoms. For"
" example you can use an upper wall on the minimum Mg—O<sub>P</sub> distance "
"to restrain it under $1~\\text{nm}$ using the "
"[`DISTANCES`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_d_i_s_t_a_n_c_e_s.html) multicolvar with the appropriate keyword."
msgstr ""
"Box 内で Ion が自由拡散する時間を省くため、Mg<sup>2+</sup> を O<sub>P</sub> "
"近傍に拘束します。例えば、[`DISTANCES`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_d_i_s_t_a_n_c_e_s.html) Multicolvar と適切な Keyword を使い、最小 "
"Mg—O<sub>P</sub> 距離に Upper Wall を設けて $1~\\text{nm}$ 未満に制限できます。"

#: PART2.md:82
msgid "Run the simulation."
msgstr "シミュレーションを実行してください。"

#: PART2.md:84
msgid ""
"In a Python notebook, plot the timeseries for the two CVs of interest as "
"well as $U_\\text{bias}(t)$."
msgstr "Python Notebook で、2つの対象 CV と $U_\\text{bias}(t)$ の時系列を描画してください。"

#: PART2.md:86
msgid "Template PLUMED file"
msgstr "PLUMED 入力のひな形"

#: PART2.md:120
msgid "![Bias test timeseries figure](solutions/figures/bias_timeseries.png)"
msgstr "![Bias テストの時系列](solutions/figures/bias_timeseries.png)"

#: PART2.md:122
msgid "Reweighting"
msgstr "Reweighting"

#: PART2.md:124
msgid ""
"If we want to recover the original statistics implied by the force field, we"
" need to reweight out the contribution of our accelerating bias. Each frame "
"of the biased trajectory will receive a weight"
msgstr ""
"Force Field が与える元の統計を復元するには、加速 Bias の寄与を Reweighting で除く必要があります。Bias 付き "
"Trajectory の各 Frame に次の重みを与えます。"

#: PART2.md:132
msgid ""
"Any observable we are interested in can then be estimated using a weighted "
"average on the $N$ frames from our biased trajectory as"
msgstr ""
"求めたい任意の Observable は、Bias 付き Trajectory の $N$ Frame の Weighted Average "
"として推定できます。"

#: PART2.md:140
msgid ""
"The quality of our estimation, however, will depend on the phase space "
"overlap between the biased and unbiased ensembles. A generic way of "
"evaluating the efficiency of our reweighting scheme is to use the Kish "
"effective sample size,"
msgstr ""
"ただし推定の質は、Bias がある Ensemble とない Ensemble の Phase Space の重なりに依存します。Reweighting"
" 効率の一般的な評価には、Kish Effective Sample Size を使います。"

#: PART2.md:148
msgid ""
"We can interpret $N_\\text{Kish}$ as the effective number of sample frames "
"that contribute to the weighted average. In the worst case scenario, "
"$N_\\text{Kish} = 1$ and only one frame has a non-zero weight, resulting in "
"a very poor estimate of $\\langle \\mathcal{O} \\rangle_{p_0}$. The higher "
"$N_\\text{Kish}$, the better the statistics, with a maximum value at "
"$N_\\text{Kish} = N$ for trivial reweighting (e.g. for a constant bias)."
msgstr ""
"$N_\\text{Kish}$ は、Weighted Average に寄与する実効的な Sample Frame 数と解釈できます。最悪の場合は "
"$N_\\text{Kish} = 1$ で、1 Frame のみが非0の重みを持つため、$\\langle \\mathcal{O} "
"\\rangle_{p_0}$ の推定は非常に悪くなります。$N_\\text{Kish}$ が高いほど統計はよくなり、自明な "
"Reweighting（一定 Bias など）では最大値 $N_\\text{Kish} = N$ になります。"

#: PART2.md:152
msgid ""
"Compute the Kish effective sample size corresponding to reweighting the "
"simulation to the original force field."
msgstr ""
"元の Force Field への Reweighting に対応する Kish Effective Sample Size を計算してください。"
